  "publicacion": {
    "titulo": "The company built to never sell bitcoin is now underwater",
    "descripcion": "Strategy (formerly MicroStrategy) held 850,364 bitcoin as of Nov 8, 2026, bought at an average of $75,456 each including fees, per its SEC 8-K filed Nov 9. On Nov 14, bitcoin traded near $64,000 (CoinDesk), below that average cost. MSCI is also removing Strategy from its indexes after the Nov 30 close, so funds that track those indexes will sell the shares; JPMorgan estimated $2.8 billion or more in outflows (CoinDesk). Strategy is not required to sell any bitcoin, but it funds new purchases by selling stock, and analysts say that just got harder. Nobody knows where bitcoin goes next. Not financial advice. 850,364 out of a 21 million maximum supply is about 1 in 25, our calculation.",
